invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh aes_runtime
reason: a QUIC host object expands an Initial key on the AES instructions
  for every ch_cfg.cpu but 0, the probe's bit alone included, so a session
  whose caller did not set CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES executes AES
  instructions before its first packet. The aes_runtime proof's stubs
  assert that only a value with the AES bit runs the instructions, over
  every 32-bit value.

--- old
    if ((cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) != 0) {
--- new
    if (cpu != 0) {
